<main>
    <section class="va-hero fade-up fade-up-2">
        <p class="va-problem">The problem</p>
        <h1 class="va-h1">Your AI tools don't share what they know about you.</h1>
        <ul class="va-bullets">
            <li>Claude Code, Claude Chat, ChatGPT, Gemini — each one starts from scratch</li>
            <li>Every project, every context, every preference: siloed by tool</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="va-divider"></div>

        <p class="va-vault-name">Parachute Vault</p>
        <p class="va-vault-desc">A self-hosted knowledge graph that lives on your machine. Every AI you use reads and writes to the same graph over MCP — notes, tags, links, project context. One source of truth your AIs actually share.</p>

        <div class="va-install">
            <div class="code-inline" style="text-align:center;">
                <code>bun add -g @openparachute/hub &amp;&amp; parachute install vault</code>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="va-cta-links">Requires <a href="https://bun.sh" target="_blank">Bun</a> &middot; <a href="/install/">Full install guide</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="va-what fade-up fade-up-3">
        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p>Run the install inside any Claude Code session — Vault is picked up automatically. Run <code>parachute expose tailnet</code> to put it on your Tailscale network, and point every other AI you use at the same HTTPS URL. They all read and write to the same graph.</p>
        <p>Notes your Claude Code session wrote are visible to ChatGPT an hour later. What you capture on your phone is context for the next chat you open on your laptop. The graph grows and connects over time — tags, wikilinks, project segments — getting richer as your AIs use it.</p>
        <p>It's a SQLite file on your disk. If we disappeared tomorrow, your graph is still there.</p>
    </section>

    <section style="max-width:640px; margin: 0 auto 4rem;">
        <div class="va-principles">
            <div class="va-pill">
                <strong>Local-first</strong>
                <span>SQLite on your disk. Nothing in the cloud unless you ask.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="va-pill">
                <strong>Open standard</strong>
                <span>Built on MCP. Works with any AI today or next year.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="va-pill">
                <strong>Open source</strong>
                <span>AGPL. Read every line of code that touches your notes.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="va-pill">
                <strong>Extensible</strong>
                <span>Small, stable service contracts. Plug in your own modules.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

